Map

Map reimplements, in Crow, the behaviour of Leaflet, Copyright the Leaflet
authors (Vladimir Agafonkin and CloudMade), licensed under the BSD
2-Clause License (https://github.com/Leaflet/Leaflet): its Web Mercator
projection, zooms and their snapping, fitBounds, flyTo, panning and
inertia, wheel, double click, keyboard, box and pinch zooms, tile ranges
and addresses, scale bar, popups, tooltips and controls. No Leaflet source
is included; its rules were read from version 1.9.4's documentation and
its numbers learned by running it, then written anew, and the sizes of its
controls, popups and tooltips were measured from its style sheet.

Mapbox GL JS was consulted only for which features a map is expected to
have (its examples); none of its code, styles or data is used. Clustering
and the heatmap are of Map's own design, and its colours are its own. No
map data is included: the example's tiles are OpenStreetMap's, fetched by
the reader's browser and credited "© OpenStreetMap contributors", and its
shapes were drawn for it.

Three parts are Lory's own, which packages/lory/NOTICE accounts for: a
polygon's fill is cut into triangles by lory.geometry (earcut's way, as
three.js cuts a shape), a move eases by lory.motion's easings, and a
marker may be drawn as one of lory.icons' pins.
